HELP=<<END
Replay commits into a numbered stack without checking out its sources
Plan commands use command=value: onto=COMMIT, pick=COMMIT or A..B, squash=COMMIT or A..B, amend=message line, drop=COMMIT, branch=00-name
Picks keep the last input commit's author and message; amend lines replace the latest output message
Squash combines changes and messages into the latest unsealed commit
Conflicts pause at STACK/rebase/work with Git's report at STACK/rebase/conflicts
Resolve the work gitlink, then continue; deleting STACK/rebase aborts the replay
Completion replaces numbered layers and preserves other stack files
@writer stack
@param stack Conversation-relative stack directory
@param [plan] STACK/rebase/plan when starting; copy a plan from elsewhere to that path first
@param [action] Use continue to resume an existing replay, without plan
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-stack --operation=rebase --help=$HELP
